18:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose-custom max-w-none","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Webflow vs Bubble vs Framer: The No-Code Showdown in 2026"]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["The no-code landscape in 2026 isn't about whether you *can* build something—it's about building the *right thing*, at the *right scale*, with the *right team*. Three platforms dominate the high-end tier: Webflow, Bubble, and Framer. But they've diverged so sharply that calling them \"competitors\" is misleading. They're adjacent disciplines wearing similar UIs."]}],["$","p","4",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Webflow remains the undisputed sovereign of design-led development. Its 2026 iteration ships with AI-powered layout suggestions, native CMS schema inference from Figma files, and seamless headless export to Next.js 15 via its new \"Bridge\" plugin system. It's not just for marketing sites anymore—enterprise clients like Patagonia and Notion's marketing arm now use Webflow as their primary content publishing layer, backed by custom React micro-frontends. Strength? Pixel-perfect control, designer autonomy, and production-grade SEO. Weakness? Anything requiring complex state management or real-time collaboration logic beyond basic forms."]}],["$","p","6",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Bubble has matured into a full-stack application platform—not just a visual backend. Its 2026 engine runs on WebAssembly-accelerated workflows, cutting latency by ~40% on heavy data operations. The new \"Logic Graph\" interface replaces nested conditionals with node-based flow orchestration (think n8n meets Airtable). Crucially, Bubble now offers optional TypeScript-compiled frontend plugins and verified AWS Lambda integrations—making it viable for regulated SaaS products (HIPAA-compliant health dashboards, FINRA-tracked fintech tools). It's no longer \"just for MVPs.\" It's for shipping v1.0—and v3.2."]}],["$","p","8",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Framer, meanwhile, has doubled down on interactivity-as-infrastructure. Its 2026 release embeds a lightweight React Server Components runtime directly in the editor, enabling dynamic server-side rendering without leaving the canvas. Animations are now timeline-agnostic and physics-based (thanks to integration with Rive 3.0), and its new \"Interaction Studio\" lets product teams record, replay, and A/B test user flows in staging—no dev handoff required. Framer isn't trying to replace your backend; it's replacing your prototyping, marketing site, and even your internal tooling layer—with zero deployment friction."]}],["$","p","10",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Here's how they stack up today:"]}],["$","div","table-22",{"className":"overflow-x-auto mb-6","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-sm border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-[#2a1a4e]","children":[["$","th","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6d3aff] border-b border-[#3b2566]","children":"Feature"}],["$","th","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6d3aff] border-b border-[#3b2566]","children":"Webflow"}],"$L1c","$L1d"]}]}],"$L1e"]}]}],"$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c"]}]
