onal SaaS"}],["$","td","3",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-[#c4b5fd]","children":"Product designers, growth marketers, startups validating UX before engineering"}]]}]]}]
1f:["$","h2","23",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#e8e0f7] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"FAQ"}]
20:["$","p","25",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#e8e0f7]","children":"Q: Can I migrate a Bubble app to Webflow or Framer?"}],""]}]
21:["$","p","26",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["A: Not meaningfully. Bubble's data model and workflow engine are deeply coupled. You can *export content* (e.g., CMS entries) but not logic or state. Think of migration as rebuilding—not porting."]}]
22:["$","p","28",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#e8e0f7]","children":"Q: Does Framer support custom code in production?"}],""]}]
23:["$","p","29",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["A: Yes—but selectively. You can inject React components (via npm packages or local files) and run client-side JS. Server logic still requires external APIs. It's \"code-aware,\" not \"code-first.\""]}]
24:["$","p","31",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#e8e0f7]","children":"Q: Is Webflow's CMS sufficient for a content-heavy SaaS dashboard?"}],""]}]
25:["$","p","32",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["A: No. Its CMS is optimized for static or semi-dynamic content—not relational, permissioned, or real-time datasets. Use Bubble or a headless CMS + Webflow frontend instead."]}]
26:["$","p","34",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#e8e0f7]","children":"Q: Which platform has the best free tier?"}],""]}]
27:["$","p","35",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["A: Framer's free tier is most generous for prototyping. Webflow's free plan is solid for static sites. Bubble's free plan includes app building but with branding and limitations."]}]
28:["$","p","37",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#e8e0f7]","children":"Q: Can I build a marketplace with these tools?"}],""]}]
29:["$","p","38",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["A: Bubble is the only viable choice for a full marketplace with user accounts, listings, payments, and messaging. Webflow and Framer lack the backend infrastructure."]}]
2a:["$","h2","40",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#e8e0f7] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"Conclusion"}]
2b:["$","p","42",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Choose Webflow if your bottleneck is design velocity, brand consistency, or content publishing—not application logic. Choose Bubble if your core challenge is building a scalable, authenticated, data-driven web product *without engineering bandwidth*. Choose Framer if your goal is to ship high-fidelity, performant, animated experiences faster than your dev team can PR—and if your users care more about feel than function."]}]
2c:["$","p","44",{"className":"text-[#c4b5fd] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Our 2026 recommendation? Start with Framer for anything customer-facing that lives at the intersection of marketing and product (landing pages, interactive demos, investor decks). Move to Bubble when you need auth, payments, or workflows that evolve with user behavior. Reserve Webflow for final-brand expression—especially when handing off to non-technical marketers who must update copy, imagery, and SEO weekly. The winner isn't the most powerful tool. It's the one that aligns with your team's muscle memory—and your company's next milestone."]}]
